        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "f14ed7fd-2594-5c2b-a182-2db4a4bef41f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John du Pont, Dave Schultz, Mark Schultz, Corey Jantzen\n- Works: Foxcatcher\n- Organizations/Teams: Team Foxcatcher, U.S. Olympic team\n- Topics: Freestyle wrestling, Olympic and world competition, wrestling choreography\n\nFacts:\n- Dave Schultz was born on June 6, 1959, and he became an American Olympic and world champion freestyle wrestler and a seven-time World and Olympic medalist.\n- In 1986, John du Pont recruited 1984 U.S. Olympic gold medalist brothers Mark Schultz and Dave Schultz to help coach U.S. wrestlers for national, world, and Olympic competition.\n- Foxcatcher is a film whose plot is loosely based on John du Pont’s recruitment of Mark Schultz and Dave Schultz and the later events surrounding them.\n- John du Pont murdered Dave Schultz in January 1996.\n- Dave Schultz died on January 26, 1996.\n- Corey Jantzen is known for his work in the Academy Award-nominated film Foxcatcher, where he played a wrestler on Team Foxcatcher and helped choreograph the wrestling sequences.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
